The one finding that matters most
From the SWE-chat extraction: github.com appears in 4,741 out of 10,673 domain events — it dominates because coding agents interact with it constantly. But the more interesting signal is the long tail: agents touch hundreds of unique domains during real work. DomainArena measures whether they understand what those services do from their names alone, which is exactly the signal that determines selection.

